## Fix

- keep `AIPage` mounted in memory after its first visit instead of unmounting it on every route change;
- hide the AI page while another section is active and show it again without resetting React state;
- preserve the selected conversation, visible messages, draft, actions and in-flight model request while moving between Home-AI pages;
- avoid starting AI API calls before the user has visited `/ai` at least once;
- add a regression test for the persistent AI-page mount policy.

This targets the live report that the current AI dialog disappears after navigating to another page and returning.

`just verify` is headed toward deterministic scope selection: it will decide what to test and check from the calling agent's workflow step. That requires a stage signal the agent cannot forge. Per the MOTOR-VARIENTE decision, the engine now injects `FABRO_STAGE=<node-id>` into every stage's agent sandbox at dispatch, and scrubs any agent-supplied value so the signal can't be spoofed.

- **Injection seam.** `FABRO_STAGE` is set at the `fabro-petri` stage-dispatch/preamble seam, alongside the existing stage env. The seed brief cited `resolve_workflow_env` in `fabro-workflow`, but no such symbol exists in the current tree — the petri dispatch seam is the real env-injection point.
- **Spoof resistance.** An agent-supplied `FABRO_STAGE` is overridden unconditionally, so a stage can't claim another node's identity to skew verification scope.
- **Tests.** Unit/e2e coverage proves `FABRO_STAGE` reaches a stage script with the correct per-node value, plus a negative test that a caller-provided value is overridden.

Consumption lands separately: `scripts/verify.nu` reading `FABRO_STAGE` (with caller-mismatch rejection and argument fallback), the justfile `verify` recipe simplification, and shrinking the develop prompts to a single `run just verify` line are loop-owner exemptions outside this change. This PR is the repo-visible engine work only.

