## English

**Problem.** Kora breaks a dependency cycle with a generated `PromisedProxy` of the dependency type. The graph accepts any non-final (Kotlin: open) class and any interface for it, but the proxy generators handle only part of such types. Otherwise the graph does not compile, the processor crashes, or the proxy silently runs a method on itself instead of on the component. Minimal reproduction (Java):

```java
@KoraApp
public interface ExampleApplication {
    class Class1 {
        public Class1(String value) {}
        public String hello() { return "hello"; }
    }
    class Class2 {
        public Class2(Class1 value) {}
    }

    default String string() { return ""; }

    @Root
    default Class1 class1(Class2 value, String string) { return new Class1(string); }

    default Class2 class2(Class1 value) { return new Class2(value); }
}
```

Result: `constructor Class1 in class ...ExampleApplication.Class1 cannot be applied to given types; required: java.lang.String, found: no arguments` in the generated `$ExampleApplication_Class1_PromisedProxy`. The other cases, all reproduced on `master`:

